perf.proposedChange:
Replace the if/else updating hi/lo with a branchless half-width step: keep a base index and a length, and on each step compare the midpoint, then advance base by (half+1) only when ptr[base+half] <= key, decrementing the remaining length accordingly. Concretely:
int baseIdx = 0; int n = len;
while (n > 1) {
  int half = n >> 1;
  int mid = baseIdx + half;
  int gt = -(ptr[mid] > key ? 0 : 1); // mask: 0 when ptr[mid] > key, -1 otherwise
  baseIdx += half & gt;
  n -= half;
}
return baseIdx + (ptr[baseIdx] <= key ? 1 : 0);
The ternaries here compile to setcc/cmov (predicated, no branch) under Burst/LLVM rather than a control-flow branch.
